-- title:
--   Origin chart ring generated by scalars, X/Y and Z/Y
-- statement:
--   Let $T$ be a commutative ring and $W$ a Weierstrass curve over $T$, read as a projective Weierstrass curve, and let $B$ be a commutative ring. Write $S = \mathrm{MvPolynomial}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\,3)\,T / (W.\mathrm{polynomial})$ for the quotient of the polynomial ring in three variables by the ideal generated by the Weierstrass cubic, graded by `projModelGradingCR W`, whose degree-$n$ piece is the image of the homogeneous polynomials of degree $n$; let `coord W i` denote the class of $X_i$, and let `OriginChartRing W` be the degree-zero homogeneous localisation `Away` of this graded ring at `coord W 1`, i.e. the coordinate ring of the chart $Y \neq 0$ containing the origin. Let $\chi,\chi' :$ `OriginChartRing W` $\to B$ be ring homomorphisms. Assume: (i) for every $t \in T$ the two maps agree on the image in the chart ring, under the canonical map `fromZeroRingHom` out of the degree-zero piece, of the scalar $t$; (ii) $\chi(\,$`xOverY W`$\,) = \chi'(\,$`xOverY W`$\,)$, the element of degree-zero fraction $X/Y$; and (iii) $\chi(\,$`zOverY W`$\,) = \chi'(\,$`zOverY W`$\,)$, the fraction $Z/Y$. Then $\chi = \chi'$.
--
--   This is the uniqueness half of the standard fact that the chart $Y \neq 0$ of the projective Weierstrass model is generated over the base by the affine coordinates $X/Y$ and $Z/Y$ at the origin $(0:1:0)$. It is used to identify ring maps out of the origin chart, for instance when comparing charts with Tate-type parametrisations and with the formal neighbourhood of the origin.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_DrinfeldGlobal_ringHom_originChartRing_ext.lean

